        "definition": "Colonization means a microorganism is present and reproducing on or in the body without causing the tissue injury and clinical response that define infection. Carriage describes the state of harboring that organism, often without symptoms. A colonized person can still transmit some organisms or later develop infection if barriers or defenses change.",
        "directTargetId": "microbiology:concept:colonization-and-carriage",
