        "name": "Foodborne transmission",
        "primaryDomain": "Microbiology",
        "searchTerms": [
          "food poisoning transmission",
          "food-borne spread",
          "foodborne outbreak",
          "Foodborne transmission"
        ],
        "sections": [
          {
            "content": "Foodborne transmission occurs when contaminated food delivers an infectious organism, parasite stage, or microbial toxin to a person.",
            "id": "definition",
            "title": "Definition"
          },
          {
            "content": "Contamination can occur during production, processing, storage, preparation, or serving. Temperature abuse may permit growth or toxin production, while inadequate cooking and cross-contamination preserve or spread the hazard.",
            "id": "mechanism",
            "title": "Mechanism"
          },
          {
            "content": "Undercooked animal products, contaminated produce, unpasteurized products, improperly canned food, and cross-contaminated ready-to-eat food involve different organisms and mechanisms.",
            "id": "examples",
            "title": "Examples"
          },
          {
            "content": "Ask what was eaten, when, who else became ill, symptom pattern, travel, and high-risk host factors; report suspected clusters through appropriate public-health channels.",
            "id": "clinical-significance",
            "title": "Clinical significance"
          },
          {
            "content": "Symptoms after a meal do not prove foodborne causation, and incubation can range from hours for preformed toxins to days or longer for infections and parasites.",
            "id": "limitations",
            "title": "Limitations"
          },
          {
            "content": "CDC foodborne-outbreak guidance connects shared food exposure, epidemiologic investigation, and laboratory evidence rather than assigning cause from timing alone.",
            "id": "sources",
            "title": "Sources"
          }
        ],
        "studentFacing": true,
