        "name": "Occupational infection controls",
        "primaryDomain": "Microbiology",
        "searchTerms": [
          "healthcare worker infection control",
          "healthcare worker vaccination",
          "needlestick prevention",
          "occupational exposure",
          "Occupational infection controls"
        ],
        "sections": [
          {
            "content": "Occupational infection controls protect healthcare workers and patients by preventing exposure, detecting risk early, and providing prompt post-exposure management.",
            "id": "scope",
            "title": "Scope"
          },
          {
            "content": "They apply to routine care, sharps, aerosols, blood or body-fluid exposure, communicable illness, laboratory work, and tasks involving hazardous decontamination products.",
            "id": "indications",
            "title": "Indications"
          },
          {
            "content": "Vaccination, engineering controls, safe devices, work practices, PPE, training, respiratory programs, health surveillance, and rapid exposure response create overlapping barriers.",
            "id": "mechanism",
            "title": "Mechanism"
          },
          {
            "content": "Know how to report an exposure immediately, obtain first aid, document the source and route, and access confidential risk assessment, testing, prophylaxis, and follow-up.",
            "id": "procedure",
            "title": "Procedure"
          },
          {
            "content": "PPE is one layer and can fail when selection, fit, donning, doffing, or disposal is incorrect. Delayed reporting can close time-sensitive prevention windows.",
            "id": "limitations",
            "title": "Limitations"
          },
          {
            "content": "Do not recap or manipulate sharps outside approved practice, and never conceal an exposure. Follow occupational-health and public-health guidance for work restrictions.",
            "id": "precautions",
            "title": "Precautions"
          },
          {
            "content": "CDC Standard Precautions and isolation recommendations place sharps safety, PPE, respiratory protection, vaccination, and exposure management within a systems approach.",
            "id": "sources",
            "title": "Sources"
          }
        ],
        "studentFacing": true,
