            "content": "Babesia microti is a clinically important protozoan parasite associated with babesiosis, hemolytic anemia, and severe babesiosis after splenectomy. The organism or agent name identifies the cause or association; it is not itself the disease diagnosis, and detection must be interpreted with the specimen, host, and syndrome.",
