            "content": "Campylobacter jejuni is a clinically important bacterium associated with acute inflammatory gastroenteritis, bacteremia, reactive arthritis, and Guillain-Barre syndrome. The organism or agent name identifies the cause or association; it is not itself the disease diagnosis, and detection must be interpreted with the specimen, host, and syndrome.",
