        "definition": "Clostridioides difficile is a Gram-positive, obligately anaerobic, spore-forming bacillus that can colonize the colon and can cause antibiotic-associated diarrhea and colitis when toxigenic strains proliferate and produce disease. Detecting the organism or one of its genes is not automatically the same as diagnosing infection; symptoms and the testing strategy must fit the clinical picture.",
