        "definition": "Human immunodeficiency virus type 1, abbreviated HIV-1, is an enveloped retrovirus that infects key immune cells, establishes lifelong infection, and without effective treatment can progressively weaken cell-mediated immunity. HIV-1 is the predominant cause of HIV infection worldwide. The virus, HIV infection, and acquired immunodeficiency syndrome are related but not identical: AIDS is the advanced clinical stage defined by severe immune suppression or specific opportunistic conditions.",
