            "content": "Mycobacterium avium complex is a clinically important bacterium associated with chronic pulmonary MAC disease, disseminated MAC in advanced immunosuppression, and cervical lymphadenitis. The organism or agent name identifies the cause or association; it is not itself the disease diagnosis, and detection must be interpreted with the specimen, host, and syndrome.",
