        "definition": "Pneumocystis jirovecii is a host-adapted fungus that causes Pneumocystis pneumonia, commonly abbreviated PCP or PJP, primarily in people with impaired cellular immunity. The older human-organism name P. carinii remains historically searchable but is no longer the preferred human species name. Detecting fungal material is not enough by itself; organism burden, specimen type, host risk, and compatible lung disease determine clinical significance.",
