        "definition": "Pseudomonas aeruginosa is a motile, nonfermenting Gram-negative bacillus found in water, soil, and moist built environments. It rarely causes disease in healthy intact tissue but becomes a formidable opportunistic pathogen when burns, devices, neutropenia, cystic fibrosis, prolonged hospitalization, or broad antibiotic exposure weaken normal barriers. Its environmental persistence and intrinsic and acquired resistance make precise culture and susceptibility testing especially important.",
